olResult","toolCallId":"toolu_014BETtQEcr8bqiqByGbbaV1","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"state_name\",\"state_abbr\"\n\"California\",\"CA\"\n\"New York\",\"NY\"\n\"Pennsylvania\",\"PA\"\n\"Minnesota\",\"MN\"\n\"Illinois\",\"IL\"\n\"Virginia\",\"VA\"\n\"Wisconsin\",\"WI\"\n\"Michigan\",\"MI\"\n\"Massachusetts\",\"MA\"\n\"Florida\",\"FL\"\n\"Georgia\",\"GA\"\n\"Ohio\",\"OH\"\n\"Texas\",\"TX\"\n\"Missouri\",\"MO\"\n\"North Carolina\",\"NC\"\n\"Iowa\",\"IA\"\n\"Kentucky\",\"KY\"\n\"Indiana\",\"IN\"\n\"Colorado\",\"CO\"\n\"Washington\",\"WA\"\n\"Maryland\",\"MD\"\n\"Connecticut\",\"CT\"\n\"Kansas\",\"KS\"\n\"Oregon\",\"OR\"\n\"Alabama\",\"AL\"\n\"Oklahoma\",\"OK\"\n\"Arizona\",\"AZ\"\n\"Tennessee\",\"TN\"\n\"South Carolina\",\"SC\"\n\"New Jersey\",\"NJ\"\n\"Montana\",\"MT\"\n\"Arkansas\",\"AR\"\n\"Louisiana\",\"LA\"\n\"Vermont\",\"VT\"\n\"Alaska\",\"AK\"\n\"Idaho\",\"ID\"\n\"West Virginia\",\"WV\"\n\"Wyoming\",\"WY\"\n\"Nebraska\",\"NE\"\n\"District Of Columbia\",\"DC\"\n\"New Hampshire\",\"NH\"\n\"Mississippi\",\"MS\"\n\"Delaware\",\"DE\"\n\"Maine\",\"ME\"\n\"New Mexico\",\"NM\"\n\"Rhode Island\",\"RI\"\n\"Utah\",\"UT\"\n\"Nevada\",\"NV\"\n\"North Dakota\",\"ND\"\n\"South Dakota\",\"SD\"\n\"Hawaii\",\"HI\"\n\"Puerto Rico\",\"PR\"\n\"Virgin Islands\",\"VI\"\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786911707562},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! I can see that the data includes:\n- 50 states + DC = 51 entries\n- Plus Puerto Rico (PR) and Virgin Islands (VI) which are territories\n\nSo I need to exclude Puerto Rico and Virgin Islands to get the total for the US excluding territories.\n\nNow I'll:\n1. Sum farmers_markets where state_abbr NOT IN ('PR', 'VI')\n2. Use the US population of 341,784,857\n3. Calculate farmers_markets_per_100k = total_farmers_markets / 341784857 * 100000\n\nLet me do this calculation.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_011rU1FPMZSHWk9TKeUWNDxr","name":"xorq_select","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog","on":"farmers_markets","compose":"source.filter((source.state_abbr != 'PR') & (source.state_abbr != 'VI')).aggregate(total_markets=source.farmers_markets.sum())"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":13,"output":284,"cacheRead":20726,"cacheWrite":597,"totalTokens":21620,"cost":{"input":0.000013,"output":0.00142,"cacheRead":0.0020726000000000004,"cacheWrite":0.00074625,"total":0.00425185},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":141},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786911707562,"responseId":"msg_011Ce73qrt7wi3BsnpwuzqWN","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_011rU1FPMZSHWk9TKeUWNDxr","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"xorq_select: select: ValueError: disallowed expression: BitAnd (the safe evaluator rejects `&`/`|` — chain filters instead: source.filter(a).filter(b))\n"}],"details":{},"isError":true,"timestamp":1786911711504},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to chain filters instead of using & operator. Let me fix that.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01RTgiXyX9kFaw3h52aAfwbk","name":"xorq_select","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog","on":"farmers_markets","compose":"source.filter(source.state_abbr != 'PR').filter(source.state_abbr != 'VI').aggregate(total_markets=source.farmers_markets.sum())"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":163,"cacheRead":21323,"cacheWrite":358,"totalTokens":21858,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.0008150000000000001,"cacheRead":0.0021323,"cacheWrite":0.0004475,"total":0.0034088},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":21},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786911711504,"responseId":"msg_011Ce73rAU3JfGS7jnydwcvg","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01RTgiXyX9kFaw3h52aAfwbk","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"total_markets\"\n7942\n\n(showing up to 50 rows; pass limit or aggregate to count — do not page)"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786911715177},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! Total farmers markets excluding territories is 7,942.\n\nNow I need to create a composition that calculates the rate per 100,000. I'll create a metric that joins these two values and computes the ratio. Let me create a build script for this cross-dataset metric.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01JvCeyZCjQFoaQpWgo4cM5e","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/farmers_markets_per_capita.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\n\n_o = u.build_opener()\n_o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]\nu.install_opener(_o)\n\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\n\n# Read farmers markets data\nfact = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"farmers_markets\",\n    storage_options=so\n)\n\n# Read census population data\nref = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"census_population\",\n    storage_options=so\n)\n\n# Get total farmers markets excluding territories (PR and VI)\nfact_total = (\n    fact.filter(fact.state_abbr != 'PR')\n        .filter(fact.state_abbr != 'VI')\n        .aggregate(total_markets=fact.farmers_markets.sum())\n        .mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n)\n\n# Get US population for 2025\nref_us = (\n    ref.filter(ref.NAME == 'United States')\n        .select('POPESTIMATE2025')\n        .mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n)\n\n# Join and calculate rate per 100,000\nexpr = (\n    fact_total.join(ref_us, fact_total.k == ref_us.k)\n        .mutate(markets_per_100k=fact_total.total_market